<title>AUSTRIA: Algeria wants $25 oil price.</title>
<headline>Algeria wants $25 oil price.</headline>
<text>
<p>VIENNA, nov 27 (Reuter) Algerian Oil Minister Amar Makhloufi said his nation wants oil prices to reach $25 a barrel but he thinks it unlikely that would happen under an emerging OPEC accord to extend its current output ceiling.</p>
<p>&quot;Prices are quite good but not enough,&quot; he told reporters. &quot;We want 25 dollars for the barrel&quot;.</p>
<p>He said an OPEC decision to extend quotas for the first six months of next year was unlikely &quot;to bring the correct price&quot;</p>
<p>He also said he did not object to the idea of a 12-month OPEC quota rollover but said OPEC was far  more likely to decide on six months.</p>
</text>
